      "writtenOn": "2026-02-23T11:18:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is just \"has_devices\" sounds very specific and I wouldn\u0027t want to reproduce the memory donation nightware where we have bool all over the place to say \"is_memory\" \"update_mmio\", \"check_refcount\" ... That makes the calls unreadable and we have the need to \"transport\" this information that could be found somewhere else.\n\nAlthough you are completely right that it forces a dependency between pviommu and guest_prepare... You could also just INIT_LIST() in pkvm_pviommu_finalise() and then pkvm_vm_has_devices() can just WARN_ON(hyp_vm.next);\n\nAlternatively, how about kvm_guest_prepare_stage2() takes the stage-2 flags as an argument? And then the caller can set the right one depending on if devices where found or not? And then a pkvm_vm_has_devices() would even be safe as we know it is called after pviommu_finalise?",
      "parentUuid": "98e9a6b0_86c28669",
